 credit_score_zscore). Measures variability in credit scores across ethnicity groups.\n# Usefulness: Identifies disparities in credit scoring standards, improving fairness in the model.\ndf['ethnicity_credit_variability'] = df.groupby('Ethnicity')['credit_score_zscore'].transform('std')", "# citizen_target_encoding\n# Target Encoded Citizenship: target_encoding(Citizen). Encodes average success rates for each citizenship category.\n# Usefulness: Helps capture the influence of citizenship status on credit application outcomes.\ncitizen_target_mean = df.groupby('Citizen')['success'].mean()\ndf['citizen_target_encoding'] = df['Citizen'].map(citizen_target_mean)", "# credit_employment_ratio\n# Credit-Employment Ratio: divide(credit_score_zscore, years_employed_zscore). Relates credit scores to standardized employment tenure.\n# Usefulness: Highlights employment instability in relation to creditworthiness.\ndf['credit_employment_ratio'] = df['credit_score_zscore'] / (df['years_employed_zscore'] + 1e-10)  # Adding epsilon to avoid division by zero", "# zscored_marital_income\n# Z-Scored Marital Income Interaction: zscore(married_income_interaction). Standardizes marital income data for fair comparisons.\n# Usefulness: Simplifies comparisons of marital income impact on credit applications across all applicants.\ndf['zscored_marital_income'] = (df['married_income_interaction'] - df['married_income_interaction'].mean()) / df['married_income_interaction'].std()", "# Drop less relevant columns\ndf.drop(columns=['compressed_income_bins', 'Gender'], inplace=True)"]
